g:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=205 valign=top style='width:153.65pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>CLINICAL\r\nNOTES<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Immunoglobulins\r\nplay a key role in the body\u2019s immune system. They are proteins produced by\r\nspecific immune cells called plasma cells in response to bacteria, viruses and\r\nother microorganisms as well as exposures to the other substances that are\r\nrecognized by the body as \u201cnon \u2013 self\u201d harmful antigens.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Immunoglobulin\r\nG (IgG) \u2013 About 70 \u2013 80% of the immunoglobulins in the blood are IgG. Specific\r\nIgG antibodies are produced during an initial infection or other antigen\r\nexposure, rising a few weeks after it begins, then decreasing and stabilizing .\r\nThe body retains a catalog of IgG antibodies that can be rapidly reproduced\r\nwhenever exposed to the same antigen. IgG antibodies form the basis of long\r\nterm protections against microorganisms . In those with a normal immune system,\r\nsufficient IgG is produced to prevent re \u2013 infection. Vaccinations use this\r\nprocess to prevent initial infections and add to the catalog of IgG antibodies,\r\nby exposing a person to weakened liver microorganism or to an antigen that\r\nstimulates recognition of the microorganism. IgG is the only immunoglobulin\r\nthat can pass through the placenta. The mother\u2019s IgG antibodies provide\r\nprotection to the fetus during pregnancy and to the baby during its first few\r\nmonths of life. There are four subclasses of IgG : IgG1, IgG2, IgG3 and IgG4.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>SIGNIFICANCE<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>-Polyclonal\r\nIgG increase is seen in SLE, Chronic liver disease, infectious diseases and\r\nCystic fibrosis.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>-Monoclonal\r\nIgG increase is seen in IgG Myelomas<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>-Decreased\r\nsynthesis of IgG is found in congenital and acquired immunodeficiency diseases\r\nand selective IgG subclass deficiency<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>-Decreased\r\nIgG levels are seen in protein losing entropathies, Nephrotic synfrome and skin\r\nburns.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"595.45pt 841.7pt","margin":"151.2pt 36.0pt 72.0pt 36.0pt"}}